title: Proposition 73
---
order: 73
---
short_label: X.73
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If from a rational straight line there is subtracted a rational straight line commensurable with the whole in square only, then the remainder is irrational; let it be called an <i>apotome.</i>
----
proof:

From the rational straight line {AB} let the rational straight line {BC}, commensurable with the whole in square only, be subtracted.

I say that the remainder {AC} is the irrational straight line called apotome.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="250" height="65" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.73 diagram" src="propX73.gif"/></noscript>
